text:
**SQL injection.** `req.params.id` goes straight into query string. Attacker passes `1 OR 1=1` → dumps all users.

**Fix — parameterized query:**

```js
app.get('/api/users/:id', async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const user = await db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1', [req.params.id]);
    if (!user) return res.status(404).json({ error: 'Not found' });
    res.json(user);
  } catch {
    res.status(500).json({ error: 'Server error' });
  }
});
```

Two more issues:
- **No auth check** — any caller gets any user's data. Add middleware to verify JWT/session and confirm `req.user.id === req.params.id` (or admin role).
- **`SELECT *`** — exposes password hashes, tokens, etc. Select only needed columns.
